<title>GERMANY: DBV-Winterthur says buys two insurers.</title>
<headline>DBV-Winterthur says buys two insurers.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>German insurer DBV Winterthur said on Monday it has purchased two insurers from its Swiss parent group in a 125 million mark ($74.9 million) transaction.</p>
<p>Winterthur said it has purchased Transatlantische Allgemeine Versicherung AG and telcon Allgemeine Versicherung AG (TRANS/telcon).</p>
<p>The purchase price included the use of what Winterthur said were &quot;considerable&quot; tax losses that will be used in 1997.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525 ($ = 1.668 German Marks)</p>
